.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_PROVIDER-FIPS 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_PROVIDER-FIPS
.Nd OpenSSL FIPS provider
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The OpenSSL FIPS provider is a special provider that conforms to the
Federal Information Processing Standards (FIPS) specified in FIPS 140-3.
This 'module' contains an approved set of cryptographic algorithms that
is validated by an accredited testing laboratory.
.Ss Properties
The implementations in this provider specifically have these properties
defined for approved algorithms:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqprovider=fips"
.It \(dqfips=yes"
.El
It may be used in a property query string with fetching functions such
as
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
or
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_fetch 3 ,
as well as with other functions that take a property query string, such
as
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name 3 .
.Pp
To be FIPS compliant, it is mandatory to include
.Qo Li fips=yes Qc
as part of all property queries.
This ensures that only FIPS approved implementations are used for
cryptographic operations.
The
.Qo Li fips=yes Qc
query may also include other non-crypto support operations that are not
in the FIPS provider, such as asymmetric key encoders, see
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-default 7 .
.Pp
It is not mandatory to include
.Qo Li provider=fips Qc
as part of your property query.
Including
.Qo Li provider=fips Qc
in your property query guarantees that the OpenSSL FIPS provider is used
for cryptographic operations rather than other FIPS capable providers.
.Ss Approved algorithms
Algorithms that are fetched using "fips=yes" may still be unapproved if
certain conditions are not met.
See
.Xr fips_module 7
for additional information.
.Ss Provider parameters
See
.Xr provider-base 7
for a list of base parameters.
The OpenSSL FIPS provider also handles FIPS indicator related parameters
as specified by
.Xr fips_config 5 .
.Sh OPERATIONS AND ALGORITHMS
