.Sh SELF TESTING
A requirement of FIPS modules is to run cryptographic algorithm self
tests.
FIPS 140-3 requires known answer tests to be run on startup as well as
conditional tests that run during cryptographic operations.
.Pp
An optional callback mechanism is available to return information to the
user using
.Xr OSSL_SELF_TEST_set_callback 3 .
.Pp
The parameters passed to the callback are described in
.Xr OSSL_SELF_TEST_new 3
.Pp
The OpenSSL FIPS module uses the following mechanism to provide
information about the self tests as they run.
This is useful for debugging if a self test is failing.
The callback also allows forcing any self test to fail, in order to
check that it operates correctly on failure.
Note that all self tests run even if a self test failure occurs.
.Pp
The FIPS module passes the following type(s) to
.Xr OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqModule_Integrity" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_MODULE_INTEGRITY )
Uses HMAC SHA256 on the module file to validate that the module has not
been modified.
The integrity value is compared to a value written to a configuration
file during installation.
.It \(dqKAT_Integrity" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_INTEGRITY )
Used during the Module Integrity test to perform a known answer test on
HMAC SHA256 prior to using it.
.It \(dqKAT_Cipher" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_CIPHER )
Known answer test for a symmetric cipher.
.It \(dqKAT_AsymmetricCipher" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_ASYM_CIPHER )
Known answer test for a asymmetric cipher.
.It \(dqKAT_Digest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_DIGEST )
Known answer test for a digest.
.It \(dqKAT_AsymmetricKeyGeneration" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_ASYM_KEYGEN )
Known answer test for asymmetric key generation.
.It \(dqKAT_Signature" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_SIGNATURE )
Known answer test for a signature.
.It \(dqPCT_Signature" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_PCT_SIGNATURE )
Pairwise Consistency check for a signature.
.It \(dqKAT_KDF" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_KDF )
Known answer test for a key derivation function.
.It \(dqKAT_KA" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_KA )
Known answer test for key agreement.
.It \(dqKAT_KEM" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_KEM )
Known answer test for key encapsulation.
.It \(dqDRBG" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_DRBG )
Known answer test for a Deterministic Random Bit Generator.
.It \(dqConditional_PCT" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_PCT )
Conditional test that is run during the generation of key pairs.
.It \(dqImport_PCT" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_PCT_IMPORT )
Conditional test that is run during the import of key pairs.
.It \(dqConditional_KAT" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_PCT_KAT )
Conditional test run during generation that derive the public key from
the private key and checks that the public key matches.
This is a SP 800-56A requirement.
.It \(dqContinuous_RNG_Test" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_CRNG )
Continuous random number generator test.
.It \(dqInstall_Integrity" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_INSTALL_INTEGRITY )
This is deprecated.
The option is no longer used since FIPS 140-3 requires self tests to
always run on startup.
Previous FIPS 140-2 validations allowed the self tests to be run just
once.
.El
.Pp
The FIPS module passes the following descriptions(s) to
.Xr OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqHMAC" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_DESC_INTEGRITY_HMAC )
"Module_Integrity" uses this.
.It \(dqRSA" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_DESC_PCT_RSA_PKCS1 )
.It \(dqRSA" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_DESC_PCT_RSA )
.It \(dqECDSA" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SELF_TEST_DESC_PCT_ECDSA )
